 "tab-baselines-1": {
  "page": 11,
  "headers": [
   [
    "Model",
    "Transformer [Vaswani et al., 2017] with convolutional positional"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "2020] and symmetric bi-directional ALiBi self-attention bias [Press et al., 2021]"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "A.6. The audio model has 24 layers, 16 attention heads, 1024/4096"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "(FFN) dimension, 330M parameters. We add skip connections connecting"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "layer to last layer, second layer to second-to-last layer, etc.)"
   ]
  ],
  "rows": [
   [
    "",
    "States are concatenated channel-wise and then combined using a linear layer."
   ],
   [
    "",
    "has 8 heads, 512/2048 embedding/FFN dimensions, with 8/10 layers for"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "(28M/34M parameters in total). All models are trained in FP16."
   ],
   [
    "Training",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "size of 240K frames. For training efficiency, audio length is capped at 1,600"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "randomly if the length exceeds this threshold. Duration models are trained for"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "effective batch size of 60K frames. The Adam [Kingma and Ba, 2014] optimizer"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "learning rate of 1e-4, linearly warmed up for 5K steps and linearly decays over"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "For audio models, we clip the gradient norm to 0.2 for training stability. The"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "is masked with pdrop = 0.3/0.2, and otherwise a segment of r% sequence"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "r ∼U[70, 100]/U[10, 100]. puncond is set to 0.2 for audio/duration models."
   ],
   [
    "Inference",
    "The torchdiffeq [Chen, 2018] package is used, which"
   ],
   [
    "",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "(NFE=32). The regression duration model is used by default. Silence at both"
   ],
   [
    "second max.",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "Baselines",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "TTS trained on Librilight. 2) YourTTS [Casanova et al., 2021], SOTA"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "and Portuguese) zero-shot TTS model trained on VCTK, LibriTTS,"
   ],
   [
    "",
    ""
   ],
   [
    "",
    "using a pre-trained multilingual speaker embedder for voice conditioning. 3)"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "SOTA for NAR speech editing and infilling trained with a regression loss on"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Demucs [Défossez et al., 2020], a SOTA speech enhancement model trained"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "adversarial losses for denoising experiments. Table 1 summarizes the tasks each"
   ],
   [
    "of solving.",
